# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SuperTile .gitignore
# Policy: deny build output, local state and anything credential-shaped.
# When in doubt, ignore it. Force-add deliberate exceptions with `git add -f`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Rust / Cargo ----------------------------------------------------------
/target/
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
*.rlib
*.rmeta
# Cargo.lock IS committed: SuperTile ships a binary, and a locked dependency
# graph is required for reproducible builds and a truthful CycloneDX SBOM.
# (EU CRA Annex I 2(1) / Annex II - see docs/compliance/EU-CRA.md)

# --- Build / packaging output ---------------------------------------------
/dist/
/out/
/build/
/pkg/
*.msi
*.msix
*.appx
*.exe
*.dll
*.obj
*.lib
*.exp
*.ilk
*.map
# Committed release artifacts that are inputs, not outputs:
!assets/**/*.ico

# --- Secrets & credentials (never commit) ----------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
*.snk
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.ppk
secrets.*
*secret*
*credential*
*password*
*.token
.netrc
_netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc
# Code-signing material for release builds
signing/
codesign/
*.spc
*.pvk

# --- Cloud / CI credentials ------------------------------------------------
.aws/
.azure/
.gcloud/
gha-creds-*.json
*serviceaccount*.json

# --- Local runtime state (SuperTile writes to %APPDATA%, but just in case) --
*.log
logs/
crash/
*.dmp
supertile.toml
supertile.json
window-memory.*
/local/
.scratch/

# --- Editors / IDEs --------------------------------------------------------
.vs/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json.example
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.user
*.suo
*.sln.docstates
.fleet/

# --- OS --------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
._*

# --- Tooling caches --------------------------------------------------------
.cargo/registry/
.cargo/git/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- Test / coverage -------------------------------------------------------
*.profraw
*.profdata
/coverage/
tarpaulin-report.*

# --- Generated compliance artifacts ----------------------------------------
# The SBOM is generated by CI but IS committed at docs/compliance/sbom.cdx.json
# so the shipped About dialog and the release tag always agree. Ignore only the
# transient copies produced in the workspace root by `cargo cyclonedx`.
/bom.json
/bom.xml
/supertile.cdx.json
/*.cdx.json
!docs/compliance/*.cdx.json
